> range of a word x
  note: "word": read as 32 bits (ARM word), not 16 bits (x86 WORD) or 64 bits (machine word) (say "16-bit", "32-bit" or "64-bit", or "assume words are 64-bit")
  ucas: it(x: u32) = x
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u32:
  0..4294967295  (sampled min/max; not a sound bound)
  fits in u32
  sampled 65536 points (domain has 4294967296 points); not exhaustive
  sound bound (intervals): 0..4294967295
  proved bound (monotonicity, exact algebra): 0..4294967295
  the sample reaches both ends: the range is exactly 0..4294967295 (proved)
    max: it is nondecreasing in x, so take x = 4294967295:
      4294967295
    min: it is nondecreasing in x, so take x = 0:
      0
> range of a 4-bit x
  note: "4-bit" without signed or unsigned: read as unsigned, u4, not signed, i4 (say "unsigned" or "signed", or "assume N-bit numbers are signed")
  ucas: it(x: u4) = x
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u4:
  0..15   (16 distinct values)
  values: 0..15
  fits in u4
  over all 16 points of the domain
> the not of x
  note: "not" of a number: read as bitwise not, ~, not logical not, ! (say "bitwise not" or "logical not")
  ucas: it(x) = ~x
  ucas: show it
  note: x has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body
it(x: int) = ~x
  -> int
> range of the integer square root of a 4-bit unsigned x
  ucas: it(x: u4) = isqrt(x)
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u4:
  0..3   (4 distinct values)
  values: 0..3
  fits in u2
  over all 16 points of the domain
